{
  "id": "zh-b1-ba",
  "category": "Mandarin B1",
  "language": "zh",
  "title": "The 把 Sentence",
  "description": "Subject + 把 + object + verb + result: what the action does to something. Why the verb can't stand alone, where 没 / 不要 go, and which verbs can't use 把.",
  "level": "B1",
  "points": [
    {
      "id": "ba_basic",
      "title": "Subject + 把 + object + verb + …",
      "summary": "把 (bǎ) moves a definite object before the verb to say what happens **to** it: put where, finished, broken, eaten ….",
      "body": "- 请**把**门关上.\n- 你**把**手机放在哪儿了?\n- 他**把**我的蛋糕吃了!",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{请|qǐng}{把|bǎ}{门|mén}{关|guān}{上|shang}。",
          "Please close the door."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ba_needs",
      "title": "The verb needs something after it",
      "summary": "A 把 sentence can't end in a bare verb: add a result (完, 好, 干净), a place (在…), 了, or a direction.",
      "body": "- 我把作业做**完了** — not ~~我把作业做~~.\n- 你把这杯水喝**了**吧.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{我|wǒ}{把|bǎ}{作业|zuòyè}{做|zuò}{完|wán}{了|le}。",
          "I've finished my homework."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ba_neg",
      "title": "没 / 不要 / modal verbs go before 把",
      "summary": "Negation and modal verbs come **before** 把, not before the verb.",
      "body": "- 我**没**把钱带来.\n- 你**不要**把这件事告诉他.\n- 你**应该**把房间打扫干净.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{你|nǐ}{不要|búyào}{把|bǎ}{这|zhè}{件|jiàn}{事|shì}{告诉|gàosu}{他|tā}。",
          "Don't tell him about this."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ba_not",
      "title": "Verbs that can't use 把",
      "summary": "Verbs that don't act on the object — 是, 有, 在, 知道, 喜欢, 觉得, 认识 — never take 把.",
      "body": "- 我很喜欢这本书 — not ~~我把这本书喜欢了~~.",
      "examples": [
        [
          "{我|wǒ}{知道|zhīdào}{这|zhè}{件|jiàn}{事|shì}。",
          "I know about this."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
